    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-7151",
      "problem": "The surface area of a cube is $240$ square units. Find the length of the edges of the cube.",
      "worked_solution": "The surface area $S$ of a cube is made of $6$ congruent squares. So, the area $\\mathcal A$ of one face is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac{S}{6} = \\frac{240}{6} = 40\\,.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathcal A = s^2,$ where $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns = \\sqrt{\\mathcal{A}} = \\sqrt{40} = 2\\sqrt{10}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $2\\sqrt{10}$ units.",
